      "blurb": "The tourist run: teamLab Planets and Borderless, tea tasting and wagashi, Meiji Shrine, the long crush of Shibuya Crossing. Figurine shopping in Akihabara, a little Harajuku fashion, and far too much convenience-store food.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "tokyo-note",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "☆☆☆ We did a pretty classic tourist run: teamLab Planets & teamLab Borderless for the digital-art wave, the Meiji Shrine for a taste of history, Akihabara for figurine shopping, and Shibuya (& Shinjuku) for shopping and nightlife. Tokyo is popping, vibrant, and endlessly fun - it felt like a crime to stay for just a week - but wonderful to know that there are endless things to explore when I return.",
          "tone": "body",
          "fontSize": {
            "large": 18,
            "medium": 18,
            "small": 16
