          "id": "hakone-note",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Our one-day trip to a Hakone ryokan. Some tatami, an onsen, and a full kaiseki dinner - an interesting experience, even if traditional Japanese food isn't my favorite. \n\n(After speaking with some younger locals, it appears there is some agreeance that parts of kaiseki are not favored, i.e. the mountain vegetables and fish parts. Much of the experience revolves around the presentation and preparation, and often reserved for special occasions. I will say I very much did enjoy the Hida beef.)",
